2026-04-17 18:31:39,104[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-808c27662fc48b40] execute_python_code({"code": "import itertools\nimport numpy as np\ndef is_valid_grid(grid):\n    # Check for T-shaped tetrominoes\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j] == 1 and grid[i+2][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j+1] == 1:\n                return False\n            if grid[i][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j+1] == 1 and grid[i][j+2] == 1:\n                return False\n            if grid[i][j] == 1 and grid[i][j+1] == 1 and grid[i][j+2] == 1 and grid[i+1][j+1] == 1:\n                return False\n            if grid[i][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j] == 1 and grid[i+1][j+1] == 1 and grid[i+2][j+1] == 1:\n                return False\n    return True\ndef find_min_k():\n    n = 7\n    max_k = n * n // 4  # Upper bound\n    for k in range(max_k, -1, -1):\n        for grid in itertools.product([0, 1], repeat=n*n):\n            grid = np.array(grid).reshape(n, n)\n            if sum(grid) == k and is_valid_grid(grid):\n                return k\n    return max_k\nmin_k = find_min_k()\nmin_k", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
